cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Sediment: How Streak Mechanics Drive Compelled Production of Low-Quality Digital Content"
message: "If you cite this concept note, please use the metadata below. A peer-reviewed version may appear later; check the related Zenodo deposit for the canonical citation once minted."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Yoon
    given-names: Jiyeon
abstract: >
  Concept note proposing 'sediment' as a category of human-generated,
  platform-compelled, demand-independent low-quality content, distinct
  from spam and AI slop. Models the lifecycle as Deposition → Compaction
  → Fossilization under streak mechanics, develops three competing
  psychological hypotheses (loss aversion, identity consistency,
  escalating commitment), and proposes four studies anchored by the
  GitHub 2016 streak-counter removal as a natural experiment.
keywords:
  - streak mechanics
  - gamification
  - content quality
  - Goodhart's Law
  - loss aversion
  - digital platforms
  - compelled production
license: CC-BY-4.0
version: 0.1.1
date-released: 2026-05-21
repository-code: "https://github.com/heznpc/sediment"
